10
00:46:04,285 --> 00:46:10,285
La La Land is a 2016 American musical romantic comedy-drama
film written and directed by Damien Chazelle.

11
00:50:40,714 --> 00:50:46,714
It stars Ryan Gosling and Emma Stone as a struggling jazz pianist and an aspiring
actress who meet and fall in love while pursuing their dreams in Los Angeles.

12
00:55:17,142 --> 00:55:23,142
The supporting cast includes John Legend,
Rosemarie DeWitt, Finn Wittrock, and J.

13
00:59:53,571 --> 00:59:59,571
Having been fond of musicals during his time as a drummer, Chazelle first conceptualized the
film alongside Justin Hurwitz while attending Harvard University together.

14
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
After moving to Los Angeles in 2010, Chazelle penned the script but did not find a
studio willing to finance the production without changes to his design.

15
01:09:06,428 --> 01:09:12,428
After the success of his film Whiplash (2014), the
project was picked up by Summit Entertainment.

16
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
Miles Teller and Emma Watson were originally in talks to star, but
after both dropped out, Gosling and Stone were cast.

17
01:18:19,285 --> 01:18:25,285
Filming took place in Los Angeles between August and September 2015, with the film's score composed by Hurwitz, who also
wrote the film's songs with lyricists Benj Pasek and Justin Paul and the dance choreography by Mandy Moore.

18
01:22:55,714 --> 01:23:01,714
La La Land premiered at the 73rd Venice International Film Festival on August 31, 2016, and
was released theatrically in the United States on December 9, by Lionsgate.

19
01:27:32,142 --> 01:27:38,142
The film emerged as a major commercial success, grossing $472 million worldwide on a budget of $30 million, and received widespread critical acclaim, particularly for
Chazelle's direction and screenplay, the performances of Gosling and Stone, the score, musical numbers, cinematography, visual style, costumes and production design.

20
01:32:08,571 --> 01:32:14,571
It went on to receive numerous accolades, including winning a record seven awards at the 74th Golden Globe Awards and
received eleven nominations at the 70th British Academy Film Awards, winning five, including Best Film.

21
01:36:45,000 --> 01:36:51,000
The film also received a record-tying fourteen nominations at the 89th Academy Awards,
winning in six categories including Best Director and Best Actress (Stone).

22
01:41:21,428 --> 01:41:27,428
Its loss in the Best Picture category (to Moonlight) made it the
most-nominated film at the Oscars to lose Best Picture.

23
01:45:57,857 --> 01:46:03,857
At age 32, Chazelle became the youngest winner of Best Director.

24
01:50:34,285 --> 01:50:40,285
It has since been regarded as one of the best films of the 2010s and the 21st
century, and as one of the best musical films of all time.

25
01:55:10,714 --> 01:55:16,714
As of February 2023, a stage musical adaptation is in the works.

26
01:59:47,142 --> 01:59:53,142
The film explores themes of dancing, dance, jazz, musical, ambition.

27
02:04:23,571 --> 02:04:29,571
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
